# Override how elements display

Use a card's **Visibility** settings to choose when it shows, and its own options to choose what it shows. Do not write CSS to hide or restyle a native card. CSS breaks when Home Assistant updates the card.

## Show a card on some screens only

Use a screen condition when a card only makes sense at some widths. For example, show a large clock on the hall wall panel but not on a phone. Do not use it to hide a control that someone needs on a phone.

```yaml
type: clock
visibility:
  - condition: screen
    media_query: "(min-width: 1024px)"
```

## Other visibility conditions

Cards, badges and sections all have visibility conditions. Find them on the **Visibility** tab in the editor.

| Condition | Shows the item when | Example |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Screen | The screen is one of the sizes you choose | A clock on the wall panel only |
| Entity state | An entity is in the state you choose | A **Close garage door** button while the garage door is open |
| Entity numeric state | A reading is above or below a number | A dehumidifier card when the bathroom humidity is above 70% |
| User | One of the people you choose is signed in | A **Server** section for the person who looks after Home Assistant |
| And, Or | All or any of several conditions are met | A frost warning on the wall panel only, when it is below 3°C |

Hide a card only when it has nothing useful to show. Do not hide the state of a lock, a door or an alarm, because people check that it is safe.

## Show less on a card

Many native cards have options that turn parts of the card off. Use them before you choose a different card.

| Card | Option | What it does |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Tile | `hide_state` | Hides the state under the name |
| Tile | `vertical` | Puts the icon above the name instead of beside it |
| Tile | `show_entity_picture` | Shows the entity's picture instead of its icon |
| Entity badge | `show_name`, `show_state`, `show_icon` | Shows or hides each part of the badge |
| Heading | `heading_style` | `title` for a section heading, `subtitle` for a smaller one |

This badge shows the name and state of the front door. Keep the name on, because a door icon alone does not say which door is open.

```yaml
type: entity
entity: binary_sensor.front_door
show_name: true
show_state: true
show_icon: true
```

A card or badge hidden by a condition or an option is hidden from screen readers too. [Hide elements and keep them accessible to screen readers](structure-hiding-elements.html) explains what to do instead.
